    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements a standalone participant-only client under `gameplay-server/remote-client/`. The API origin remains empty and unapproved; no guessed hostname or usable public configuration is included.\n\n- Uses only participant `GET /v1/battles/{battleId}` and `POST /v1/battles/{battleId}/commit`.\n- Keeps bearer tokens in page memory by default; IndexedDB retention is opt-in and locally removable.\n- Preserves pending command identity and selection for safe retry; pending state is isolated by battle and bearer digest, including atomic same-token multi-tab get-or-create.\n- Validates public server views before applying them or deleting pending command records.\n- Reveals opponent selections only after server-authorized reveal.\n- Uses the approved Chat01 labels without changing API codes or game rules.\n- Guards async restore, connect, refresh, Remember, Forget and commit work with session/request epochs. Forget invalidates synchronously.\n\n## Historical sequence audit\n\n**HISTORICAL PRE-PUBLICATION REVIEW: FAIL.** Draft PR #451 was first opened at 2026-10-28T15:39:05Z before exact-diff review reported the trailing-dot origin denylist bypass. Later reviews and fixes are post-publication; they are not represented as preliminary review. No duplicate PR was created and history was not rewritten.\n\nRepository rules require review and required checks before merge. The repository authority I read does not make exact-diff review before PR creation a non-overridable publication gate. This historical ordering failure remains recorded; no exception was needed under the applicable repository rules.\n\n## Current evidence\n\n- Exact HEAD: `f20145bb5b5188dd33ea5f00a80eb421f87daaae`, parent/base main: `31b7a077820914e92de81239e5ab4099e3dfa558`.\n- Local remote-client regressions: `REMOTE_CLIENT_TESTS_PASS 32/32`, including approved labels; deterministic Forget during restore/connect/refresh/commit; concurrent same-token IndexedDB command creation; malformed GET/POST views; out-of-order refresh; expiry and timeout recovery.\n- Local offline hosted-D1 harness safety tests: 22/22. Syntax checks and `git diff --check` pass.\n- Exact-HEAD GitHub checks and independent review are running for `f20145bb5b5188dd33ea5f00a80eb421f87daaae`.\n\nNo Worker, SQL, D1 schema, production CORS, Stage 7.15, deployment or Cloudflare resource changes. No remote Safari or production-authentication claim. Physical two-device and separate staging acceptance remain outstanding.",
